**EXECUTE NOW. Fix 2 pages + create 2 new files. No planning replies.**

Two dynamic route pages currently fail to build because `"use client"` conflicts with `generateStaticParams`. Split each into server page + client subcomponent.

## Files to fix at `/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/Marketing Site/InkOS/`:

### Pattern A: `src/app/customers/[slug]/`

Currently `page.tsx` is `"use client"` with motion + generateStaticParams. Build error.

**Fix:**

1. NEW `src/app/customers/[slug]/customer-story-detail.tsx` (`"use client"`)
   - Takes props: `{ story: CustomerStory; related: CustomerStory[] }`
   - Contains ALL the JSX currently in page.tsx body (motion.h1, motion.div, etc)
   - Imports motion, fadeUp, stagger from framer-motion + brand
   - Renders Nav/Footer/main/sections — entire page body
   - Type: `interface Props { story: CustomerStory; related: CustomerStory[]; }`

2. REPLACE `src/app/customers/[slug]/page.tsx` with server component:
```tsx
import { notFound } from "next/navigation";
import { customerStories } from "@/lib/data/customer-stories";
import { CustomerStoryDetail } from "./customer-story-detail";
import type { Metadata } from "next";

interface PageProps {
  params: Promise<{ slug: string }>;
}

export function generateStaticParams() {
  return customerStories.map((s) => ({ slug: s.slug }));
}

export async function generateMetadata({ params }: PageProps): Promise<Metadata> {
  const { slug } = await params;
  const story = customerStories.find((s) => s.slug === slug);
  if (!story) return {};
  return {
    title: `${story.name} — ${story.role} | InkOS`,
    description: story.shortQuote.slice(0, 160),
    openGraph: {
      title: `${story.name} runs ${story.role.split('·')[1]?.trim() ?? "their studio"} on InkOS`,
      description: story.shortQuote,
      type: "article",
    },
    alternates: { canonical: `https://inkos.studio/customers/${slug}` },
  };
}

export default async function Page({ params }: PageProps) {
  const { slug } = await params;
  const story = customerStories.find((s) => s.slug === slug);
  if (!story) notFound();

  const related = story.similarStudios
    .map((rs) => customerStories.find((s) => s.slug === rs))
    .filter((s): s is NonNullable<typeof s> => Boolean(s))
    .slice(0, 2);

  return <CustomerStoryDetail story={story} related={related} />;
}
```

### Pattern B: `src/app/blog/[slug]/`

Same fix:

1. NEW `src/app/blog/[slug]/blog-post-detail.tsx` (`"use client"`)
   - Takes props: `{ post: BlogPost; related: BlogPost[] }`
   - Contains ALL existing JSX from page.tsx including ContentBlock helper

2. REPLACE `src/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx` with server component:
```tsx
import { notFound } from "next/navigation";
import { blogPosts } from "@/lib/data/blog-posts";
import { BlogPostDetail } from "./blog-post-detail";
import type { Metadata } from "next";

interface PageProps {
  params: Promise<{ slug: string }>;
}

export function generateStaticParams() {
  return blogPosts.map((p) => ({ slug: p.slug }));
}

export async function generateMetadata({ params }: PageProps): Promise<Metadata> {
  const { slug } = await params;
  const post = blogPosts.find((p) => p.slug === slug);
  if (!post) return {};
  return {
    title: `${post.title} | InkOS Blog`,
    description: post.excerpt,
    openGraph: {
      title: post.title,
      description: post.excerpt,
      type: "article",
      publishedTime: post.publishedAt,
      authors: [post.author.name],
    },
    alternates: { canonical: `https://inkos.studio/blog/${slug}` },
  };
}

export default async function Page({ params }: PageProps) {
  const { slug } = await params;
  const post = blogPosts.find((p) => p.slug === slug);
  if (!post) notFound();

  const related = blogPosts
    .filter((p) => p.slug !== slug && p.category === post.category)
    .slice(0, 3);

  return <BlogPostDetail post={post} related={related} />;
}
```

## Implementation steps

1. Read existing `src/app/customers/[slug]/page.tsx` — extract ALL JSX from `<div ...><Nav />...</div>` 
2. Move that JSX into a new `customer-story-detail.tsx` as a `"use client"` component named `CustomerStoryDetail` accepting `story` + `related` as props
3. Replace original page.tsx with server template above
4. Same for blog: read `src/app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx`, move ALL JSX (including the `ContentBlock` helper function) into new `blog-post-detail.tsx`, replace page.tsx with server template

Both detail subcomponents stay client side. Both new server pages use `async/await params` instead of `use(params)`.

In the server pages, do NOT import React for `use` — just `await params`.

In the client detail subcomponents, import `notFound` is no longer needed there (handled in server page).

## Verification

After all 4 file edits/creations: `cd "/Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/Marketing Site/InkOS" && pnpm run build`. Must pass with all routes static. Report PASS or paste errors.

WRITE THE 4 FILES NOW.

